{"case_id":"T8011","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["archive_read_open_filenames","archive_read_set_switch_callback","archive_read_set_callback_data2","archive_read_add_callback_data","archive_read_append_callback_data","archive_read_prepend_callback_data","archive_read_open1","client_switch_proxy","client_close_proxy","__archive_read_filter_ahead","advance_file_pointer","file_open","file_switch","file_close2"],"reason":"H0 fuzzes only a single contiguous memory object through archive_read_open_memory. S1 adds multivolume input through a NULL-terminated filename array and through indexed callback-data nodes, including automatic source switching at per-node EOF, explicit switch callbacks or close/open fallback, aggregate cleanup, and index-dependent mutation APIs. Those protocols and boundary states cannot be exercised by H0, so malformed archives split across volumes, empty or failing volumes, switching failures, node ordering/index errors, and data spanning volume boundaries are fuzz-worthy uncovered surfaces.","evidence":["H0 calls archive_read_open_memory(a, image, size) once per mutation and never calls archive_read_open_filenames or any callback-data/switch API.","archive_read_open_filenames builds multiple read_file_data nodes with archive_read_append_callback_data and installs file_switch via archive_read_set_switch_callback.","__archive_read_filter_ahead and advance_file_pointer now call client_switch_proxy when a read returns zero and client.cursor is not client.nodes - 1, creating new EOF-transition behavior absent from the single-memory-input harness.","client_switch_proxy changes client.cursor and filter->data, then invokes archive_switch_callback or a closer/opener fallback; H0 supplies neither multiple data nodes nor this callback lifecycle.","archive_read_set_callback_data2 and archive_read_add_callback_data introduce index validation and dynamic dataset allocation/reallocation, while prepend and append alter node ordering; H0 exercises none of these state transitions.","client_close_proxy iterates over every client.dataset node, and archive_read_open1 opens dataset[0] and may close all nodes after an open failure, adding multi-node error and cleanup paths not reached by H0."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated stateful multivolume fuzz target that partitions fuzz bytes into a variable number of volumes and exercises both archive_read_open_filenames and the callback API. Vary node count, ordering, empty volumes, split points, valid and invalid indices, callback return codes, switch-callback presence versus close/open fallback, and reads/skips that cross volume boundaries; then drain headers and data and always close/free the archive."}
